    {
      "id": 4,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"preparation\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Research replacing the O(P·k) sorted-array insertion in src/knn.c with a bounded max-heap, targeting O(P log k). Preserve the baseline’s stable handling of equal distances by ranking candidates on (squared distance, original encounter index); benchmark across input sizes and k values, and verify output correctness rather than assuming a speedup.\",\"B\":\"Research CPU parallelization suited to the measured ARM64 target (4 cores, no GPU): partition the encountered points into contiguous ranges, compute private top-k candidate sets, then deterministically merge them using the same distance-and-encounter-order ranking as the baseline. Measure thread overhead and end-to-end performance; use only mechanisms compatible with the existing build setup.\",\"C\":\"Research an introselect-based alternative for regimes where k is large relative to P: compute candidate records, select the first k by (squared distance, encounter index), and tally their labels without sorting all P candidates. Assess its O(P) extra-memory cost and worst-case behavior; compare correctness and timings against the baseline and the other approaches.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidate programs produced by A/B/C. First measure each candidate independently, then measure the integrated program as a whole—do not assume gains add. Preserve exact classification behavior, including distance ties and vote ties, and select or dispatch among approaches only when correctness and end-to-end measurements support it. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions.\",\"analysis\":\"The current source is Problem A’s KNN classifier. Its baseline scans P points and may inspect/shift up to k entries per point, then sorts k labels; squared Euclidean distances avoid square roots. The sole automatic measurement is a correct baseline (4 cases), mean 2.0356777108584843 seconds over three runs [2.0604070760309696, 2.0158473001793027, 2.03077875636518], score 0.5. No candidate or integration measurements are provided, so these are research hypotheses, not demonstrated improvements. All approaches must remain general and preserve baseline tie behavior.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"7f1d4b9792fb9d74c5c647c8bdfc37f28fc8a0ed2dea1141ea5219f26e2b21f5\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Research replacing the O(P·k) sorted-array insertion in src/knn.c with a bounded max-heap, targeting O(P log k). Preserve the baseline’s stable handling of equal distances by ranking candidates on (squared distance, original encounter index); benchmark across input sizes and k values, and verify output correctness rather than assuming a speedup.\",\"B\":\"Research CPU parallelization suited to the measured ARM64 target (4 cores, no GPU): partition the encountered points into contiguous ranges, compute private top-k candidate sets, then deterministically merge them using the same distance-and-encounter-order ranking as the baseline. Measure thread overhead and end-to-end performance; use only mechanisms compatible with the existing build setup.\",\"C\":\"Research an introselect-based alternative for regimes where k is large relative to P: compute candidate records, select the first k by (squared distance, encounter index), and tally their labels without sorting all P candidates. Assess its O(P) extra-memory cost and worst-case behavior; compare correctness and timings against the baseline and the other approaches.\",\"G\":\"Integrate only candidate programs produced by A/B/C. First measure each candidate independently, then measure the integrated program as a whole—do not assume gains add. Preserve exact classification behavior, including distance ties and vote ties, and select or dispatch among approaches only when correctness and end-to-end measurements support it. Do not alter tests, oracle, compiler, budgets, target, or permissions.\",\"analysis\":\"The current source is Problem A’s KNN classifier. Its baseline scans P points and may inspect/shift up to k entries per point, then sorts k labels; squared Euclidean distances avoid square roots. The sole automatic measurement is a correct baseline (4 cases), mean 2.0356777108584843 seconds over three runs [2.0604070760309696, 2.0158473001793027, 2.03077875636518], score 0.5. No candidate or integration measurements are provided, so these are research hypotheses, not demonstrated improvements. All approaches must remain general and preserve baseline tie behavior.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"b70b4f38c3a147049e18c7b5852a6d73\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"7f1d4b9792fb9d74c5c647c8bdfc37f28fc8a0ed2dea1141ea5219f26e2b21f5\",\"session_id\":\"bb7a58941e74486ba24267f2f526de8f\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"2846bdfd7f182fe277550d244f121215fb0f1573a8e04f49991d77158e468086\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":4224,\"input_tokens\":10898,\"output_tokens\":4888,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":4446}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":15786,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
