      "id": 17,
      "kind": "mother_usage",
      "payload": "{\"model_calls\":1,\"phase\":\"synthesis\",\"plan\":{\"A\":\"Use the measured heap implementation as the reference and investigate a hybrid serial top-k selector: retain a simple ordered-array path where k is small, and use a bounded max-heap otherwise. Choose any crossover from general workload measurements, not test-specific values. Preserve strict distance ties by encounter order, underfilled-k sentinel behavior, voting ties, and baseline behavior for values that do not have a total heap ordering.\",\"B\":\"Explore removing the post-selection qsort of labels: tally counts over the char domain, then scan in the same numeric order as compare_for_sort so equal vote counts select the same label. Include sentinel labels when fewer than k points are available. The memmove variant remained near baseline time, while the SIMD search was slower; avoid spending effort repeating those approaches unless new measurements motivate it.\",\"C\":\"Investigate whether parallel distance scanning can beat the serial heap on the ARM64 four-core target. The recorded private-heap OpenMP variant took about 0.0330 s versus about 0.0270 s for the fastest serial candidate, so focus on reducing team/setup and merge overhead, and use a general workload-based threshold with a serial fallback. Preserve deterministic distance-and-encounter ordering and baseline edge behavior; do not assume parallel execution wins.\",\"G\":\"Integrate candidate programs conservatively. The lowest recorded mean is candidate 4e5248ae712349b9 at about 0.0270 s; candidate 718bf7eca1eb4d80 is close at about 0.0277 s. Treat these as performance leads, not correctness assumptions: gate on oracle correctness, compare complete integrated builds, and measure each combination independently. In particular, do not assume combining SoA, heap, or OpenMP changes gives additive gains.\",\"analysis\":\"Problem A evaluates one query against all points. The baseline scans up to k slots and shifts candidates for each point, giving O(P·k) selection work. The strongest measured result is the SoA-plus-heap candidate at 0.0270 s, compared with the 2.0357 s baseline. The other heap candidate is similarly fast; the memmove change barely improves baseline time (2.0133 s), and the SIMD variant regresses to 3.7608 s. The parallel candidates at 0.0330–0.0344 s are slower than the fastest serial candidate on this target. Preserve the sequential implementation's observable behavior, including tie ordering, label-vote tie handling, underfilled-k padding, and any cases where distance comparisons are not a total order. These measurements are guidance, not a guarantee that candidate combinations will perform well.\"},\"request_sha256\":\"39c46e97d919ab1230e27dcb423bceb89c875968dd9f315ecd514cd1438bf6ba\",\"response\":{\"data\":{\"A\":\"Use the measured heap implementation as the reference and investigate a hybrid serial top-k selector: retain a simple ordered-array path where k is small, and use a bounded max-heap otherwise. Choose any crossover from general workload measurements, not test-specific values. Preserve strict distance ties by encounter order, underfilled-k sentinel behavior, voting ties, and baseline behavior for values that do not have a total heap ordering.\",\"B\":\"Explore removing the post-selection qsort of labels: tally counts over the char domain, then scan in the same numeric order as compare_for_sort so equal vote counts select the same label. Include sentinel labels when fewer than k points are available. The memmove variant remained near baseline time, while the SIMD search was slower; avoid spending effort repeating those approaches unless new measurements motivate it.\",\"C\":\"Investigate whether parallel distance scanning can beat the serial heap on the ARM64 four-core target. The recorded private-heap OpenMP variant took about 0.0330 s versus about 0.0270 s for the fastest serial candidate, so focus on reducing team/setup and merge overhead, and use a general workload-based threshold with a serial fallback. Preserve deterministic distance-and-encounter ordering and baseline edge behavior; do not assume parallel execution wins.\",\"G\":\"Integrate candidate programs conservatively. The lowest recorded mean is candidate 4e5248ae712349b9 at about 0.0270 s; candidate 718bf7eca1eb4d80 is close at about 0.0277 s. Treat these as performance leads, not correctness assumptions: gate on oracle correctness, compare complete integrated builds, and measure each combination independently. In particular, do not assume combining SoA, heap, or OpenMP changes gives additive gains.\",\"analysis\":\"Problem A evaluates one query against all points. The baseline scans up to k slots and shifts candidates for each point, giving O(P·k) selection work. The strongest measured result is the SoA-plus-heap candidate at 0.0270 s, compared with the 2.0357 s baseline. The other heap candidate is similarly fast; the memmove change barely improves baseline time (2.0133 s), and the SIMD variant regresses to 3.7608 s. The parallel candidates at 0.0330–0.0344 s are slower than the fastest serial candidate on this target. Preserve the sequential implementation's observable behavior, including tie ordering, label-vote tie handling, underfilled-k padding, and any cases where distance comparisons are not a total order. These measurements are guidance, not a guarantee that candidate combinations will perform well.\"},\"error\":null,\"infrastructure_error\":false,\"model\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"nonce\":\"8af2ad8b0e7d46bdbec1a734700e0c2f\",\"protocol\":\"hpc-forest-codex-mailbox-v1\",\"reasoning_effort\":\"max\",\"request_sha256\":\"39c46e97d919ab1230e27dcb423bceb89c875968dd9f315ecd514cd1438bf6ba\",\"session_id\":\"bb7a58941e74486ba24267f2f526de8f\",\"usage\":{\"cached_tokens_included_in_input\":true,\"codex_jsonl_sha256\":\"e3e1c5e163d95aa8cca8ed4c485cff43c21a82e0544ca694ee47325efae8a7ed\",\"events\":[{\"cache_write_input_tokens\":0,\"cached_input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens\":23658,\"output_tokens\":5421,\"reasoning_output_tokens\":4873}],\"llm_calls\":1,\"model_requested\":\"gpt-6-luna\",\"reasoning_effort_requested\":\"max\",\"token_accounting\":\"exact\",\"tokens\":29079,\"tool_events\":[]}},\"status\":\"complete\"}",
